    {
      "x": 5,
      "y": 6,
      "type": "dialog",
      "label": "THE LOGBOOK",
      "prompt": "PRESS E TO READ",
      "dialog": "THIS YEAR'S LOG, OPEN UNDER THE LAMP. WIND, WEATHER, SHIPS PASSING, OIL BURNED - IN A SMALL, STEADY HAND.\n\nTHEN, EVERY NIGHT FOR THREE WEEKS, ONE MORE LINE:\n'LIGHT ANSWERED FROM MIDNIGHT, NORTH BY EAST. THREE LONG, ONE SHORT.'"
    },
    {
      "x": 5,
      "y": 2,
      "type": "dialog",
      "label": "OLD LOGS",
      "prompt": "PRESS E TO READ",
      "dialog": "FORTY YEARS OF LOGBOOKS, SPINES FADED TO THE SAME GREY-BLUE.\n\nONE IS MARKED WITH A RIBBON. AN OLDER HAND, THE NIGHT OF A GREAT STORM: 'MORNING TIDE NOT IN. LAMP KEPT ALL NIGHT. LIGHT ANSWERED FROM MIDNIGHT - THREE LONG, ONE SHORT.' THEN NOTHING ABOUT IT EVER AGAIN.\n\nSIGNED E. GALE."
    },
    {
      "x": 3,
      "y": 5,
      "type": "dialog",
      "label": "KEEPER'S BED",
      "prompt": "PRESS E TO LOOK",
      "dialog": "MADE TIGHT AS A DRUM, A SAPPHIRE-AND-GOLD QUILT. NOBODY HAS SLEPT IN IT FOR WEEKS.\n\nA BOOK FACE DOWN ON THE PILLOW: 'SIGNALS AND CALLS OF THE LUMAR FLEET'."
    },
    {
      "x": 3,
      "y": 7,
      "type": "dialog",
      "label": "SEA CHEST",
      "prompt": "PRESS E TO LOOK",
      "dialog": "PAINTED ON THE LID, NEARLY WORN AWAY: 'M. GALE - MORNING TIDE'.\n\nIT'S LOCKED."
    },
    {
      "x": 8,
      "y": 4,
      "type": "dialog",
      "label": "STOVE",
      "prompt": "PRESS E TO LOOK",
      "dialog": "AN IRON STOVE, BANKED LOW. THE KETTLE ON IT IS STILL WARM.\n\nSOMEBODY COMES DOWN TO FILL IT."
    },
    {
      "x": 8,
      "y": 6,
      "type": "dialog",
      "label": "OIL DRUMS",
      "prompt": "PRESS E TO LOOK",
      "dialog": "DRUMS OF LAMP OIL, STENCILLED 'SAPPHIRE LIGHT - KEEPER'S USE'. TWO ARE EMPTY.\n\nAT THIS RATE THE LAMP'S BURNING HOTTER THAN IT NEEDS TO."
    },
    {
      "x": 3,
      "y": 8,
      "type": "dialog",
      "label": "OILSKINS",
      "prompt": "PRESS E TO LOOK",
      "dialog": "A YELLOW OILSKIN AND SOU'WESTER ON A PEG. THE COAT IS DRY AND STIFF - NOT WORN SINCE THE LAST RAINS."
    },
    {
      "x": 8,
      "y": 9,
      "type": "dialog",
      "label": "CRATE",
      "prompt": "PRESS E TO LOOK",
      "dialog": "SPARE WICKS, A TIN OF BRASS POLISH, A DOZEN CANDLE ENDS, AND A SMALL BLUE CRYSTAL WRAPPED IN A CLOTH, LIKE SOMETHING PUT AWAY FOR LATER."
    },
    {
      "x": 3,
      "y": 3,
      "type": "dialog",
      "label": "WINDOW",
      "prompt": "PRESS E TO LOOK",
      "dialog": "THE NIGHT SEA, AND A WHITE MOON.\n\nTHE BEAM SWEEPS OVER THE WATER ABOVE YOU, BLUE, AND BLUE, AND BLUE."
    }
  ],
